name: code-task
description: |
  Use when: a general coding task (feature, bug fix, refactor) should go from
  requirements to a validated change: gather requirements, plan, review the plan,
  write failing tests, implement, validate.

  Requirements come from an Azure DevOps work item when one is referenced and the
  azure-ado MCP is connected; otherwise the workflow interviews you.

  Work item reference formats (first match wins):
    1. --input work_item=1234   or   --input work_item=<work item URL>
    2. A work item URL in the message:
         https://dev.azure.com/{org}/{project}/_workitems/edit/1234
         https://{org}.visualstudio.com/{project}/_workitems/edit/1234
    3. AB#1234 in the message (Azure Boards mention syntax)
  A bare "#1234" is NOT treated as a work item.

  ADO project: taken from the URL, else --input ado_project=<name>, else the
  AZURE_PROJECT Doppler secret (applied by chezmoi). If the azure-ado MCP is missing/disconnected or no
  project resolves, the workflow falls back to the interview and says why. Once the
  MCP is confirmed, a failed fetch (not found, auth, wrong org) fails the run. A
  fetched work item is checked against the code, glossary and ADRs; one with gaps
  (e.g. no acceptance criteria) or conflicts goes to the interview to resolve
  them. The workflow never writes to the board.

  Every path produces one proposal.md (problem, outcome, acceptance criteria as
  GIVEN/WHEN/THEN scenarios with AC-n IDs, invariants, decisions) that the rest
  of the run works from.

  Planning discovers the repo's own test/lint/build/typecheck commands and runs
  them once as a baseline (pre-existing failures are recorded, and only new ones
  count later). It then loops: plan (one task per test-first cycle, traced to
  AC IDs; verification steps instead of tests in repos without tests), an
  independent review (up to 3 rounds), and your approval: Approve plan, Revise
  plan, or Back to interview. Proposal issues the planner finds also reopen the
  interview.

  Before building, you choose: commit after each task, once at the end, or not
  at all. Each task then runs test-first: its tests are written and proven to
  fail, it is implemented (up to 3 attempts) until they pass unchanged, and the
  repo's checks must show no failures beyond the baseline's. Repos without
  tests skip the test steps; lint/build/typecheck still run. A task that cannot
  be completed stops at a gate: retry with your guidance, re-check after your
  own fix, or abort.

  Validation reruns every check against the baseline and runs four separate
  reviews: acceptance (each AC traced to evidence, plus behavior no test
  covers), quality, security, and error handling. Behavior tests do not cover
  becomes verification steps: manual instructions, plus an explained script you
  can choose to have run. Findings stop at a gate: Fix, Accept as-is, or Abort.

  Finally, glossary terms and ADRs (the AI decides what qualifies) are written
  to $DOCS_DIR, uncommitted; report.md records what was delivered, with each AC
  and its evidence; and if the branch has commits, you are offered a draft PR
  (GitHub or Azure DevOps), which pushes the branch only on your approval.

  Interactive: the run pauses at gates for your answers, so launch it in the
  foreground. Requirements and planning are read-only.

interactive: true

# The run commits and may push, so it always works on its own branch.
worktree:
  enabled: true

inputs:
  work_item:
    default: ""
    description: ADO work item ID (1234) or work item URL. Overrides any reference in the message.
  ado_project:
    default: {{ (dopplerProjectJson).AZURE_PROJECT | default "" | quote }}
    description: ADO project for bare IDs and AB# references. Defaults to the AZURE_PROJECT Doppler secret.
  projects_dir:
    default: {{ .projectPath | default "" | quote }}
    description: >-
      Folder holding your local projects; agents look for other repos here and
      never search the whole filesystem. Defaults to chezmoi's projectPath.

returns: write-report

nodes:
  - id: intake
    script: intake
    runtime: bun
    timeout: 60000
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        source:          { type: string, enum: [ado, interview] }
        work_item_id:    { type: string }
        project:         { type: string }
        request:         { type: string }
        fallback_reason: { type: string }
      required: [source, work_item_id, project, request, fallback_reason]

  - id: fetch-ado
    command: fetch-ado
    depends_on: [intake]
    when: "$intake.output.source == 'ado'"
    provider: claude
    model: small
    allowed_tools:
      - mcp__azure-ado__wit_get_work_item
      - mcp__azure-ado__wit_get_work_items_batch_by_ids
      - mcp__azure-ado__wit_list_work_item_comments
      - Write
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        fetched:                 { type: boolean }
        error:                   { type: string }
        has_acceptance_criteria: { type: boolean }
        gaps:                    { type: array, items: { type: string } }
      required: [fetched, error, has_acceptance_criteria, gaps]

  # Fails the run when the fetch failed or the artifact is missing; otherwise
  # records the ticket's gaps (ticket-gaps.md) for the interview.
  - id: check-fetch
    script: check-fetch
    runtime: bun
    depends_on: [fetch-ado]
    with:
      fetched: "$fetch-ado.output.fetched"
      error: "$fetch-ado.output.error"
      has_acceptance_criteria: "$fetch-ado.output.has_acceptance_criteria"
      gaps: "$fetch-ado.output.gaps"
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        gaps: { type: array, items: { type: string } }
      required: [gaps]

  # Checks the ticket against the code, context files, glossary and ADRs.
  # Read-only; writes ticket-conflicts.md when it finds any.
  - id: reconcile-ticket
    command: reconcile-ticket
    depends_on: [check-fetch]
    model: medium
    context: fresh
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        conflicts: { type: array, items: { type: string } }
      required: [conflicts]

  - id: ticket-ready
    script: ticket-ready
    runtime: bun
    depends_on: [check-fetch, reconcile-ticket]
    with:
      gaps: "$check-fetch.output.gaps"
      conflicts: "$reconcile-ticket.output.conflicts"
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        complete: { type: boolean }
      required: [complete]

  # Runs for interview-sourced work and for tickets with gaps or conflicts;
  # complete tickets skip it. Read-only: writes only $ARTIFACTS_DIR files. Each
  # round pauses at the gate; choosing Ready ends the loop.
  - id: interview
    depends_on: [intake, ticket-ready]
    trigger_rule: none_failed_min_one_success
    when: "$intake.output.source == 'interview' || $ticket-ready.output.complete == false"
    loop_group:
      nodes:
        # $LOOP_PREV is not substituted inside command files, so the previous
        # gate's answer is passed in as a binding ($INPUTS.reply).
        - id: interview-round
          command: interview
          with:
            reply: "$LOOP_PREV.interview-gate.output.text"
        - id: interview-gate
          depends_on: [interview-round]
          approval:
            message: "$interview-round.output"
            decisions:
              - { id: approve, label: "Send answers" }
              - { id: ready, label: "Ready: write proposal" }
      until_bash: test $interview-gate.output.decision = ready
      max_iterations: 20

  - id: write-proposal
    command: write-proposal
    depends_on: [interview]
    context: fresh

  - id: proposal-from-ticket
    command: proposal-from-ticket
    depends_on: [ticket-ready]
    when: "$ticket-ready.output.complete == true"
    context: fresh

  # Join point for every path. proposal.md is the single brief all later
  # nodes read; everything up to here is read-only.
  - id: check-proposal
    script: check-proposal
    runtime: bun
    depends_on: [write-proposal, proposal-from-ticket]
    trigger_rule: none_failed_min_one_success
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        acceptance_criteria: { type: array, items: { type: string } }
        unresolved:          { type: array, items: { type: string } }
      required: [acceptance_criteria, unresolved]

  # ── Planning ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Finds the repo's own commands; "" means none found. has_tests false means
  # tasks carry verification steps instead of tests.
  - id: discover-toolchain
    command: discover-toolchain
    depends_on: [check-proposal]
    model: small
    context: fresh
    allowed_tools: [Read, Glob, Grep]
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        has_tests: { type: boolean }
        test:      { type: string }
        lint:      { type: string }
        build:     { type: string }
        typecheck: { type: string }
      required: [has_tests, test, lint, build, typecheck]

  # Runs the commands on the untouched branch. Pre-existing failures are
  # recorded (baseline.md + logs), not fatal: validation judges only new ones.
  - id: baseline
    script: baseline
    runtime: bun
    depends_on: [discover-toolchain]
    timeout: 1800000
    with:
      test: "$discover-toolchain.output.test"
      lint: "$discover-toolchain.output.lint"
      build: "$discover-toolchain.output.build"
      typecheck: "$discover-toolchain.output.typecheck"
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        red: { type: array, items: { type: string } }
      required: [red]

  # One pass: clarify with the requester if needed, plan, check, review, and
  # your approval. Repeats until you approve. "Back to interview" or proposal
  # issues raised by the planner reopen the interview on the next pass.
  - id: planning
    depends_on: [baseline]
    loop_group:
      nodes:
        - id: prepare-clarify
          script: prepare-clarify
          runtime: bun
          when: "$LOOP_PREV.check-plan.output.has_issues == true || $LOOP_PREV.plan-approval.output.decision == 'revise-requirements'"
          with:
            feedback: "$LOOP_PREV.plan-approval.output.text"

        - id: clarify
          depends_on: [prepare-clarify]
          loop_group:
            nodes:
              - id: clarify-round
                command: clarify
                with:
                  reply: "$LOOP_PREV.clarify-gate.output.text"
              - id: clarify-gate
                depends_on: [clarify-round]
                approval:
                  message: "$clarify-round.output"
                  decisions:
                    - { id: approve, label: "Send answers" }
                    - { id: ready, label: "Ready: update proposal" }
            until_bash: test $clarify-gate.output.decision = ready
            max_iterations: 20

        - id: revise-proposal
          command: revise-proposal
          depends_on: [clarify]
          context: fresh

        - id: recheck-proposal
          script: check-proposal
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [revise-proposal]
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              acceptance_criteria: { type: array, items: { type: string } }
              unresolved:          { type: array, items: { type: string } }
            required: [acceptance_criteria, unresolved]

        - id: plan
          command: plan
          depends_on: [recheck-proposal]
          with:
            approval_response: "$LOOP_PREV.plan-approval.output"
          trigger_rule: all_done
          model: large
          context: fresh

        - id: check-plan
          script: check-plan
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [plan]
          with:
            has_tests: "$discover-toolchain.output.has_tests"
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              has_issues: { type: boolean }
            required: [has_issues]

        # Independent review; stops when approved or after 3 rounds, so open
        # findings reach your gate instead of failing the run.
        - id: plan-review
          depends_on: [check-plan]
          when: "$check-plan.output.has_issues == false"
          loop_group:
            nodes:
              - id: review-plan
                command: review-plan
                model: large
                context: fresh
                output_format:
                  type: object
                  properties:
                    approved: { type: boolean }
                    findings: { type: array, items: { type: string } }
                  required: [approved, findings]
              - id: revise-plan
                command: revise-plan
                depends_on: [review-plan]
                when: "$review-plan.output.approved == false"
              - id: review-round
                script: review-round
                runtime: bun
                depends_on: [revise-plan]
                trigger_rule: all_done
                output_format:
                  type: object
                  properties:
                    round: { type: number }
                  required: [round]
            until_bash: test $review-plan.output.approved = true || test $review-round.output.round -ge 3
            max_iterations: 4

        - id: final-check-plan
          script: check-plan
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [plan-review]
          with:
            has_tests: "$discover-toolchain.output.has_tests"
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              has_issues: { type: boolean }
            required: [has_issues]

        - id: gate-summary
          script: gate-summary
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [final-check-plan]

        - id: plan-approval
          depends_on: [gate-summary]
          approval:
            message: "$gate-summary.output"
            decisions:
              - { id: approve, label: "Approve plan" }
              - { id: revise-plan, label: "Revise plan" }
              - { id: revise-requirements, label: "Back to interview" }
      # Whole output, not .decision: the gate is skipped on passes where the
      # planner raised proposal issues, and a field read on a skipped node fails.
      until_bash: >-
        printf '%s' $plan-approval.output | grep -Eq '"decision": *"approve"'
      max_iterations: 5

  # ── Build ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Asked once, before any code is written. Commits never include $DOCS_DIR
  # or files the baseline left behind.
  - id: commit-mode
    depends_on: [planning]
    approval:
      message: "How should the workflow commit the change?"
      decisions:
        - { id: approve, label: "Commit after each task" }
        - { id: end, label: "Commit once at the end" }
        - { id: none, label: "Don't commit" }

  # One pass per task attempt. Repos with tests: write the task's tests, prove
  # they fail, implement until they pass (up to 3 attempts) with baseline-
  # relative regression checks. Repos without tests: implement, then lint/
  # build/typecheck. A task that cannot be completed goes to the stuck gate.
  - id: build
    depends_on: [commit-mode]
    loop_group:
      nodes:
        - id: next-task
          script: next-task
          runtime: bun
          with:
            has_tests: "$discover-toolchain.output.has_tests"
            stuck_gate: "$LOOP_PREV.stuck-gate.output"
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              done_all: { type: boolean }
              task_id:  { type: string }
              phase:    { type: string }
            required: [done_all, task_id, phase]

        - id: write-tests
          command: write-tests
          depends_on: [next-task]
          when: "$next-task.output.phase == 'tests'"
          context: fresh
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              test_command: { type: string }
              test_files:   { type: array, items: { type: string } }
            required: [test_command, test_files]

        # Runs every pass (red is "ready to implement"), so nothing downstream
        # reads a skipped producer.
        - id: red-check
          script: red-check
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [write-tests]
          trigger_rule: all_done
          timeout: 1800000
          with:
            test_command: { from: "$write-tests.output.test_command", if_skipped: "" }
            test_files: { from: "$write-tests.output.test_files", if_skipped: "[]" }
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              red: { type: boolean }
            required: [red]

        - id: implement-task
          depends_on: [red-check]
          when: "$red-check.output.red == true"
          loop_group:
            nodes:
              - id: implement
                command: implement
                context: fresh
              - id: green-check
                script: green-check
                runtime: bun
                depends_on: [implement]
                timeout: 3600000
                with:
                  has_tests: "$discover-toolchain.output.has_tests"
                  baseline_red: "$baseline.output.red"
                  test: "$discover-toolchain.output.test"
                  lint: "$discover-toolchain.output.lint"
                  build: "$discover-toolchain.output.build"
                  typecheck: "$discover-toolchain.output.typecheck"
                output_format:
                  type: object
                  properties:
                    green:       { type: boolean }
                    needs_judge: { type: boolean }
                    judge:       { type: array, items: { type: string } }
                  required: [green, needs_judge, judge]
              - id: regression-judge
                command: regression-judge
                depends_on: [green-check]
                when: "$green-check.output.needs_judge == true"
                context: fresh
                output_format:
                  type: object
                  properties:
                    new_failures: { type: array, items: { type: string } }
                  required: [new_failures]
              - id: green-verdict
                script: green-verdict
                runtime: bun
                depends_on: [regression-judge]
                trigger_rule: all_done
                with:
                  green: "$green-check.output.green"
                  needs_judge: "$green-check.output.needs_judge"
                  new_failures: { from: "$regression-judge.output.new_failures", if_skipped: "[]" }
                output_format:
                  type: object
                  properties:
                    green:    { type: boolean }
                    attempts: { type: number }
                  required: [green, attempts]
            until_bash: test $green-verdict.output.green = true || test $green-verdict.output.attempts -ge 3
            max_iterations: 4

        - id: finish-task
          script: finish-task
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [implement-task]
          trigger_rule: all_done
          when: "$next-task.output.done_all == false"
          with:
            commit_mode: "$commit-mode.output"
            docs_dir: "$DOCS_DIR"
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              done:      { type: boolean }
              committed: { type: boolean }
            required: [done, committed]

        - id: stuck-summary
          script: stuck-summary
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [finish-task]
          when: "$finish-task.output.done == false"

        # Must stay the body's only terminal node to pause the loop. Abort is
        # acted on by next-task at the start of the following pass.
        - id: stuck-gate
          depends_on: [stuck-summary]
          approval:
            message: "$stuck-summary.output"
            decisions:
              - { id: approve, label: "Retry with guidance" }
              - { id: recheck, label: "I fixed it, re-check" }
              - { id: abort, label: "Abort run" }
      until_bash: test $next-task.output.done_all = true
      max_iterations: 60

  # ── Validation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # One pass per round of fixes: apply the fixes you asked for, rerun every
  # check against the baseline, four independent reviews (separate command
  # files so each can be tuned on its own), verification steps for what tests
  # do not cover, then the findings gate. Ends when a pass finds nothing or
  # you choose Accept as-is.
  - id: validation
    depends_on: [build]
    loop_group:
      nodes:
        - id: validation-start
          script: validation-start
          runtime: bun
          with:
            findings_gate: "$LOOP_PREV.findings-gate.output"
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              fix: { type: boolean }
            required: [fix]

        - id: apply-fixes
          command: apply-fixes
          depends_on: [validation-start]
          when: "$validation-start.output.fix == true"
          context: fresh

        - id: commit-fixes
          script: commit-fixes
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [apply-fixes]
          with:
            commit_mode: "$commit-mode.output"
            docs_dir: "$DOCS_DIR"
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              committed: { type: boolean }
            required: [committed]

        - id: final-checks
          script: final-checks
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [validation-start, commit-fixes]
          trigger_rule: all_done
          timeout: 3600000
          with:
            has_tests: "$discover-toolchain.output.has_tests"
            baseline_red: "$baseline.output.red"
            test: "$discover-toolchain.output.test"
            lint: "$discover-toolchain.output.lint"
            build: "$discover-toolchain.output.build"
            typecheck: "$discover-toolchain.output.typecheck"
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              failures:    { type: array, items: { type: string } }
              needs_judge: { type: boolean }
              judge:       { type: array, items: { type: string } }
            required: [failures, needs_judge, judge]

        - id: final-judge
          command: regression-judge
          depends_on: [final-checks]
          when: "$final-checks.output.needs_judge == true"
          context: fresh
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              new_failures: { type: array, items: { type: string } }
            required: [new_failures]

        - id: review-acceptance
          command: review-acceptance
          depends_on: [final-judge]
          trigger_rule: all_done
          model: large
          context: fresh
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              findings: &findings
                type: array
                items:
                  type: object
                  properties:
                    severity: { type: string, enum: [high, medium, low] }
                    summary:  { type: string }
                    evidence: { type: string }
                  required: [severity, summary, evidence]
              uncovered: { type: array, items: { type: string } }
            required: [findings, uncovered]

        - id: review-quality
          command: review-quality
          depends_on: [final-judge]
          trigger_rule: all_done
          context: fresh
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              findings: *findings
            required: [findings]

        - id: review-security
          command: review-security
          depends_on: [final-judge]
          trigger_rule: all_done
          model: large
          context: fresh
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              findings: *findings
            required: [findings]

        - id: review-errors
          command: review-errors
          depends_on: [final-judge]
          trigger_rule: all_done
          context: fresh
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              findings: *findings
            required: [findings]

        - id: verification-setup
          script: verification-setup
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [review-acceptance]
          with:
            has_tests: "$discover-toolchain.output.has_tests"
            uncovered: "$review-acceptance.output.uncovered"
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              needed: { type: boolean }
            required: [needed]

        - id: prepare-verification
          command: prepare-verification
          depends_on: [verification-setup]
          when: "$verification-setup.output.needed == true"
          context: fresh

        # Rounds until every step has a result. Passed results are kept across
        # validation passes; nothing scripted runs without your say-so.
        - id: verification
          depends_on: [prepare-verification]
          loop_group:
            nodes:
              - id: record-verification
                command: record-verification
                with:
                  gate_response: "$LOOP_PREV.verify-gate.output"
                when: "$LOOP_PREV.verify-gate.output.decision == 'approve' || $LOOP_PREV.verify-gate.output.decision == 'results'"
                context: fresh
              - id: verification-status
                script: verification-status
                runtime: bun
                depends_on: [record-verification]
                trigger_rule: all_done
                output_format:
                  type: object
                  properties:
                    pending: { type: number }
                    message: { type: string }
                  required: [pending, message]
              - id: verify-gate
                depends_on: [verification-status]
                when: "$verification-status.output.pending > 0"
                approval:
                  message: "$verification-status.output.message"
                  decisions:
                    - { id: approve, label: "Run these scripts" }
                    - { id: results, label: "Here are my manual results" }
            until_bash: test $verification-status.output.pending -eq 0
            max_iterations: 20

        - id: findings-summary
          script: findings-summary
          runtime: bun
          depends_on: [verification, review-quality, review-security, review-errors]
          trigger_rule: all_done
          with:
            check_failures: "$final-checks.output.failures"
            new_failures: { from: "$final-judge.output.new_failures", if_skipped: "[]" }
            acceptance: "$review-acceptance.output.findings"
            uncovered: "$review-acceptance.output.uncovered"
            quality: "$review-quality.output.findings"
            security: "$review-security.output.findings"
            errors: "$review-errors.output.findings"
          output_format:
            type: object
            properties:
              clean:   { type: boolean }
              count:   { type: number }
              message: { type: string }
            required: [clean, count, message]

        # Must stay the body's only terminal node. Fix and Abort are acted on
        # by validation-start at the start of the next pass.
        - id: findings-gate
          depends_on: [findings-summary]
          when: "$findings-summary.output.clean == false"
          approval:
            message: "$findings-summary.output.message"
            decisions:
              - { id: approve, label: "Fix" }
              - { id: accept, label: "Accept as-is" }
              - { id: abort, label: "Abort run" }
      until_bash: >-
        test $findings-summary.output.clean = true ||
        printf '%s' $findings-gate.output | grep -Eq '"decision": *"accept"'
      max_iterations: 6

  # No-op unless "Commit once at the end" was chosen; runs after validation so
  # the commit includes any fixes.
  - id: commit-end
    script: commit-end
    runtime: bun
    depends_on: [validation]
    with:
      commit_mode: "$commit-mode.output"
      docs_dir: "$DOCS_DIR"
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        committed: { type: boolean }
      required: [committed]

  # ── Close-out ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Glossary and ADRs go to $DOCS_DIR after the change is settled; the AI
  # decides what qualifies as an ADR. Never committed by the workflow.
  - id: docs-start
    script: docs-start
    runtime: bun
    depends_on: [commit-end]

  - id: write-docs
    command: write-docs
    depends_on: [docs-start]
    model: large
    context: fresh
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        glossary_terms: { type: array, items: { type: string } }
        adrs:           { type: array, items: { type: string } }
      required: [glossary_terms, adrs]

  - id: check-docs
    script: check-docs
    runtime: bun
    depends_on: [write-docs]
    with:
      docs_dir: "$DOCS_DIR"

  - id: write-report
    command: write-report
    depends_on: [check-docs]
    context: fresh

  - id: check-report
    script: check-report
    runtime: bun
    depends_on: [write-report]

  # A draft PR is offered only when the branch has commits. Opening one pushes
  # the branch, so it sits behind your approval.
  - id: pr-check
    script: pr-check
    runtime: bun
    depends_on: [check-report]
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        commits: { type: number }
        forge:   { type: string }
        branch:  { type: string }
      required: [commits, forge, branch]

  - id: pr-gate
    depends_on: [pr-check]
    when: "$pr-check.output.commits > 0"
    approval:
      message: |
        This branch has $pr-check.output.commits commit(s) on $pr-check.output.branch ($pr-check.output.forge).
        Open a draft pull request? This pushes the branch. The report becomes the PR description.
      decisions:
        - { id: approve, label: "Open a draft PR" }
        - { id: skip, label: "Don't open a PR" }

  - id: pr-decision
    script: pr-decision
    runtime: bun
    depends_on: [pr-gate]
    with:
      pr_gate: "$pr-gate.output"
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        open: { type: boolean }
      required: [open]

  - id: open-pr
    command: open-pr
    depends_on: [pr-decision]
    when: "$pr-decision.output.open == true"
    provider: claude
    context: fresh
    output_format:
      type: object
      properties:
        url:   { type: string }
        error: { type: string }
      required: [url, error]
